      "provenance_score": 1.0,
      "content_sha256": "1253e24f754886a045d95e88162a8f566faf14e2be63a93f1f8c029da3b6fe64"
    },
    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "Ordinarily, a more circuitous route to the estimation of $ \\rho_{E} $ is necessary. The usual approach is to estimate the phenotypic and genetic correlations first, and to extract the environmental correlation from the algebraic relationship between the three quantities. The phenotypic correlation between two traits is easily acquired, as it is simply the correlation of the measures of the two traits in the same individual,",
      "source_page": 650,
      "printed_page": 630,
      "source_block_ids": [
        "Genetics_chapter21:p010:b2"
