    },
    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "The derivation of Equation 21.12 assumes zero covariance between the genetic value of trait 1 in individual x and the environmental deviation of trait 2 in relative y, and vice versa, a reasonable assumption if maternal effects can be ruled out. This problem aside, it should also be emphasized that because Equations 21.6, 21.7, and 21.9 only provide approximations of the additive genetic correlation, Equation 21.12 yields only an approximation of the environmental correlation. All of the nonadditive genetic variance and covariance that is not included in the estimation of $ \\rho_{A} $ will contribute to $ \\rho_{E} $. For example, when the genetic covariance is estimated by twice the covariance of offspring and midparents, the actual composition of the excess “environmental” covariance is",
